.TH PATH_RELATIVE_B 3
.SH NAME
path_relative_b \- compute a relative path from a buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "int path_relative_b(const char* " path ", size_t " len ", stralloc* " out ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_relative_b
converts a path specified by a pointer
.I path
and length
.I len
into a path relative to the current working directory, appending the result to the
.B stralloc
pointed to by
.IR out .
.PP
The function internally retrieves the current working directory using
.BR path_getcwd (3),
compares it against the provided path, and calculates the necessary navigation steps (e.g., using ".." components) to describe the target path relative to the process's current location.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 1 on success, or 0 if the path could not be converted or an error occurred during path resolution.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR path_relative (3),
.BR path_relative_to_b (3),
.BR path_getcwd (3)